
This project implements an Arduino-based Smart Automated Clothes Dryer Controller engineered for precision temperature and humidity regulation during fabric drying cycles.

Multi-Zone Sensing: 
Uses dual DHT22 sensors and dual DS18B20 waterproof probes to monitor average chamber temperature and relative humidity.

Adjustable Thermal Profiles: 
Features a selector knob (potentiometer) allowing users to choose drying temperatures ($30^\circ\text{C}$ to $70^\circ\text{C}$) based on fabric type (delicates, cottons, heavy fabrics).

Closed-Loop Actuation:
Heater & Air Blower (Pins 11 & 12): 
Engages targeted heat and hot air circulation when chamber temperature is below target.
Exhaust Fan (Pin 10): 
Evacuates excess moisture and heat once the target threshold is reached to accelerate drying efficiency and prevent thermal damage to clothes.
